  "query_preview": "dry weather will be worsening drought conditions, as \nrainfall deficits will increase over the next 7 days. The increasing \nprevalence of drought could leave the region susceptible to enhanced \nfire weather conditions, particularly as falling leaves increases \nthe amount of 1- and 10-hr fuels present. Fortunately, we should \ncontinue to see fairly good recovery of RH values at night, at least \nthrough mid-week, and current 10-hr fuel moisture from local obs \nsites are in the 11-13% range, above critical levels. The Hot-Dry-\nWindy Index (HDWI) does approach the 75th percentile of \nCFSR climatology by mid-week, though in general, relatively light \nwinds will limit the overall fire danger across the area.\n\nBy Halloween weekend, a pattern shift will begin to take place, as \nsuccessive shortwaves break down the ridging across the eastern US. \nAs one of these waves crosses east of the Mississippi over the \nweekend, moisture return should lead to increasing rain chances \nacross the area. Between 60-80% of GEFS/ECMWF/CMC ensemble members \nhave measurable precipitation at some point over the weekend, with \nthe Euro featuring faster timing in general with better rain chances \non Halloween. This pattern shift should continue into the first week \nof November, when ensemble guidance continues to favor a more active \nand dynamic pattern across the eastern US.",
